5565,"type":"genre","name":"Symphonic Prog","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":52427769209791,"name":"Doom, super-doom y stoner rock","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2000,"desc":"El doom (exageración lenta, gótica y barroca de los grooves de Black Sabbath) crece en Inglaterra: Paradise Lost, Cathedral (las largas suites líricas de Forest Of Equilibrium), My Dying Bride y Electric Wizard, que infla la pesadez hasta que la música ya no fluye, solo retumba (Come My Fanatics, Dopethrone); Orange Goblin, Katatonia. El «super-doom» de los Melvins sigue en Seattle con Earth (drones colosales entre La Monte Young y monstruos extraterrestres), Karp, Sunn, y el «sludgecore» del Sur (Eyehategod, Harvey Milk). El stoner rock: Kyuss, Queens Of The Stone Age, Sleep, Fu Manchu, Monster Magnet, Wellwater Conspiracy, Boris.","color":"#f87171","family":"Hard rock, metal y grunge","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#stoner-doom"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":59388003826898,"artist":"Cathedral","artist_id":167909820776543,"title":"Forest Of Equilibrium","year":1991,"ess":0,"yt":"EZkufellkew","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Doom, super-doom y stoner rock","scene_id":52427769209791,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#stoner-doom","chapters":["Sección 6.16"],"pages":[[1,288,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":288,"text":"…progressively more sophisticated groups. Paradise Lost, who debuted with Paradise Lost (1990), were the least creative of the founding fathers, but Cathedral (1), featuring vocalist Lee Dorrian (ex-Napalm Death), invented a new format with the lengthy and lyrical suites of Forest Of Equilibrium (1991),…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Expansion of Doom Atmosphere (90s-00s)","